@startuml issue8-sequence-diagram
' Issue #8 / PR #79: what happens when the manager opens the full Edit Product
' flow and then clicks Save. Mirrors handleSubmit in product-edit-full-form.tsx.

title Issue #8 - Full Edit Product Flow: Open and Save

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF3C4
skinparam noteBorderColor #D9A400
skinparam participant {
  BackgroundColor #EEEEEE
  BorderColor #777777
  BackgroundColor<<new>> #C8E6C9
  BorderColor<<new>> #2E7D32
  BackgroundColor<<modified>> #FFE0B2
  BorderColor<<modified>> #E65100
}
autonumber

actor Manager
participant "ProductGeneralSection" as Detail <<modified>>
participant "ProductEditFull" as Route <<new>>
participant "ProductEditFullForm" as Form <<new>>
participant "utils.ts" as Utils <<new>>
participant "sdk.admin.upload" as Upload
participant "useBatchProductVariants" as BatchHook <<new>>
participant "useLinkProductOptions" as LinkHook
participant "useProductVariantsInventoryItemsBatch" as InvHook
participant "useUpdateProduct" as UpdateHook
database "Medusa Backend" as Backend

== Part 1: Opening the flow ==

Manager -> Detail : click "Edit Product"
Detail -> Route : navigate to products/:id/edit-all
Route -> Backend : useProduct, useStore, useRegions,\nusePricePreferences
Backend --> Route : product, store, regions, price preferences
note right of Route
  The form is only rendered once ALL four queries
  have returned, because its default values are
  computed once on first render.
end note
Route -> Form : render(product, store, regions, pricePreferences)
Form -> Utils : mapProductToFormValues(product)
Utils --> Form : pre-filled form values
note right of Form
  Every field is pre-filled from the stored product.
  Nothing is written to the server while the manager
  moves through the tabs (Details, Organize, Variants,
  Inventory kits). Closing the modal just discards the
  form after the unsaved-changes prompt.
end note

== Part 2: Saving ==

Manager -> Form : click Save on the last tab
Form -> Form : handleSubmit(values)

opt new image files were added
  Form -> Upload : create({ files })
  alt upload fails
    Upload --> Form : error
    Form -> Manager : error toast, stop
    note right of Form
      Unlike the create flow, we stop here. Carrying on
      would silently drop the images the manager just
      added.
    end note
  else upload succeeds
    Upload --> Form : uploaded URLs
    Form -> Form : swap temporary preview URLs\nfor uploaded URLs
  end
end

Form -> Utils : buildProductEditRequests(values, product, media)
Utils --> Form : ProductEditRequests
note right of Utils
  Diffs the form against the stored product. Only the
  parts that changed are present, so the steps below
  are skipped when their payload is undefined.
end note

group Requests sent in a fixed order (stop at the first failure)
  opt variantDeletes present
    Form -> BatchHook : mutateAsync({ delete })
    BatchHook -> Backend : batch variants (delete)
    Backend --> BatchHook : ok
    note right of BatchHook
      Deletes get their own request and run FIRST. A batch
      runs create, update and delete in parallel, and the
      backend refuses to unlink an option value while a
      variant still uses it.
    end note
  end

  opt optionsAdd present
    Form -> LinkHook : mutateAsync(optionsAdd)
    LinkHook -> Backend : link new options and values
    Backend --> LinkHook : ok
    note right of LinkHook
      New options and values must exist before any variant
      created or updated next refers to them.
    end note
  end

  opt variantsBatch present
    Form -> BatchHook : mutateAsync({ create, update })
    BatchHook -> Backend : batch variants (create, update)
    Backend --> BatchHook : ok
    note right of BatchHook
      New hook: the existing useUpdateProductVariantsBatch
      could only update. It also invalidates the variant,
      product and inventory caches.
    end note
  end

  opt inventoryItems present
    Form -> InvHook : mutateAsync(inventoryItems)
    InvHook -> Backend : update inventory kit links
    Backend --> InvHook : ok
  end

  opt optionsRemove present
    Form -> LinkHook : mutateAsync(optionsRemove)
    LinkHook -> Backend : unlink unused option values
    Backend --> LinkHook : ok
    note right of LinkHook
      Option values are only unlinked once nothing uses
      them any more, so this runs after the variants are
      updated.
    end note
  end

  Form -> UpdateHook : mutateAsync(requests.product)
  UpdateHook -> Backend : update product fields
  Backend --> UpdateHook : ok
  note right of UpdateHook
    The product's own fields go last.
  end note
end

alt all requests succeeded
  Form -> Manager : success toast, close modal\n(handleSuccess)
else any request failed
  Form -> Backend : invalidate product query (refetch)
  Form -> Manager : error toast, modal stays open
  note right of Form
    Earlier requests may already be saved, so the product
    is refetched to show what is really stored. The modal
    stays open so the manager can retry.
  end note
end

legend right
  |= Color |= Meaning |
  |<#EEEEEE>   | Existing code |
  |<#FFE0B2>   | Modified by this issue |
  |<#C8E6C9>   | New in this issue |
endlegend

@enduml
